WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.119
Week 11: Food, Markets, and Restaurants. buy food order a meal handle dietary needs and problems

2
00:00:07.119 --> 00:00:13.940
Cultural lens. Markets, tipping, menus del día, regional staples, and meal etiquette.

3
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:26.011
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:26.011 --> 00:00:37.869
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:37.869 --> 00:00:46.869
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:46.869 --> 00:01:18.823
Model language. La propina no es obligatoria en todos los países. — The tip isn't mandatory in every country. Cada mesero espera un trato distinto. — Each server expects different treatment. Los platos típicos varían por región. — Typical dishes vary by region. Compartir comida es común en muchas culturas. — Sharing food is common in many cultures. El horario de comida cambia mucho entre países. — Meal schedules change a lot between countries.

7
00:01:18.823 --> 00:01:28.742
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
